# Vendored third-party sources, and where each came from.
#
# This file is the record that scripts/update-vendored.sh checks the tree
# against, so a vendored dependency cannot quietly stop matching the release it
# claims to be. Hand-editing a version here does not update anything -- it makes
# `update-vendored.sh verify` fail until the files are actually refreshed, which
# is the point.
#
# Columns, pipe-separated:
#   name        directory under third_party/
#   repo        GitHub owner/name
#   tag         the release tag, verbatim (tag schemes differ between projects)
#   assets      files published as RELEASE ASSETS, space-separated
#   repofiles   files taken from the REPO TREE at that tag, space-separated
#
# ada publishes its amalgamation only as release assets -- upstream's
# singleheader/ directory holds the generator, not the generated files -- while
# the licence exists only in the tree. Hence the two columns.

ada | ada-url/ada | v4.0.0 | ada.cpp ada.h ada_c.h | LICENSE-MIT
